d ISM better than probably  anything else was a little plaque that  reads did you know that up to 85 kinds  of dinosaurs were on the ark including  two tyrannosaurids - Stegosaurus - sarah  top seeds and - Brachiosaurus so yeah I  love that that's just that is a classic  example of Hammond ISM in case you  needed one I'm an American I care a lot  about freedom of speech I care a lot  about the right to assemble I care a lot  about separation of church and state I  care a lot about a freedom of religion  so I'm okay with the first two purposes  of the Ark Encounter just so long as  it's not funded by taxes or the  government and not promoted by the  public school system the third purpose  of the Ark Encounter by my account is to  preach Hammond ISM all throughout the  Ark there were all kinds of displays  that were designed to convert skeptics  whether they be outside of  she anity altogether you know  non-religious folks or whether they be  Christians that are not also Hema  Knights  Ken Ham is trying to convert people to  his way of thinking about Genesis let me  be clear he's not trying to like take  people from their religions and make  them get baptized into his own special  religion instead he's trying to get  people from various Christian  backgrounds to accept the special new  non biblical doctrines that he's  produced his unique additions to the  book of Genesis these include baby  t-rexes on Noah's Ark and extremely  rapid speciation or hyper evolution  after Noah's Flood he's doing work with  the Baptist Southern Baptist Convention  trying to make sure that they get on  board get on board no pun intended  the fourth purpose of the Ark Encounter  is one that did bother me I care deeply  about science education I care deeply  about scientific literacy of my fellow  citizens and the fourth purpose of the  Ark Encounter was to spread anti science  propaganda and conspiracy theories on  the third floor of the Ark Encounter are  where Ken Ham has most of his scientific  claims about animals and geology and the  age of the earth and so on in future  videos I'll show you that many of his  displays were either misleading or in  some cases blatantly incorrect and not  only that but a lot of them were  spreading conspiracy theories really  pitting the viewer against science in  general now that there are a lot of  Christians they don't have any issues  with science at all a lot of a lot of  people even the science of evolution  there are a lot of Christians that have  no problem with it there are some  Christians that have an issue with  evolution but they don't really have an  issue with other branches of science but  Ken Ham really seemed to be anti science  in general  he had particularly there was one part  let me read this to you this is from Ken  hams Mars exhibit and he talks about the  discovery that Mars seems to have once  had an ocean that covered part of its  surface in the distant past  we of course no longer find liquid water  on Mars one of his plaque says why do so  many scientists reject a massive flood  on earth while accepting one on Mars the  truth is that the world wide flood  described in Genesis would completely  undermine evolutionary beliefs about  life on this planet the rejection of the  Biblical Flood is often due to  evolutionary biases rather than the  actual evidence in fact it is not a  stretch to think that nearly every  geologist would appeal to a global flood  to explain many of Earth's features if  the Bible had never mentioned such an  event in this plaque he is making a huge  conspiracy theory claim he is saying  that scientists all around the world  from China to the Middle East to you  know Canada and the United States  everybody is teaming up to attack the  Bible scientists everywhere are teaming  up to attack the Bible first of all  that's completely not true there are  tons of  scientists that are Christians huge  numbers of scientists are Christians but  that is just a horrible horrib